:\nprint(get_planet_names())\n```\n\nWhen you run this code, it will output:\n\n```json\n[\"mercury\",\"venus\",\"earth\"]\n```\n\nThis function uses Python's built-in `json` module to convert the list of planet names into a JSON array. The result is then returned as a string.","calls":[],"prompt_tokens":27,"cached_tokens":30,"generated_tokens":181,"prefill_ms":720,"decode_ms":19703},{"id":"extraction","status":"pass","content":"March 14","reasoning_chars":0,"raw":"March 14","calls":[],"prompt_tokens":85,"cached_tokens":30,"generated_tokens":3,"prefill_ms":2435,"decode_ms":403},{"id":"memory-across-turns","status":"pass","content":"Bagwis","reasoning_chars":0,"raw":"Bagwis","calls":[],"prompt_tokens":23,"cached_tokens":85,"generated_tokens":2,"prefill_ms":743,"decode_ms":243},{"id":"tool-call","status":"pass","content":"","reasoning_chars":0,"raw":"<|python_tag|>{\"name\": \"get_weather\", \"parameters\": {\"city\": \"Manila\"}}","calls":[{"name":"get_weather","arguments":"{\"city\": \"Manila\"}"}],"prompt_tokens":189,"cached_tokens":5,"generated_tokens":18,"prefill_ms":6249,"decode_ms":2363},{"id":"tool-result","status":"fail","content":"","reasoning_chars":0,"raw":"<|python_tag|>{\"name\": \"get_weather\", \"parameters\": {\"city\": \"Manila\"}}","calls":[{"name":"get_weather","arguments":"{\"city\": \"Manila\"}"}],"prompt_tokens":27,"cached_tokens":212,"generated_tokens":18,"prefill_ms":879,"decode_ms":2191}]}
